course: dictionary
lesson: 11986
title: Cessation: the formal word for stop
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal. They appear in news reports, law, medicine and exams, and they sound careful and serious. Cessation is one of them. It means the stopping or ending of something. «The cessation of the rain let the children play outside.» The rain stopped, so cessation means stopping.
explain: Look for the thing that stopped. In «smoking cessation», the thing that stops is smoking. Use the swap check: «stopping smoking» makes good sense, so cessation must mean stopping.
explain: In everyday talk you would say stop or end. A formal word like cessation tells you the writer is being careful or official. Cessation is a noun, so you can say «a cessation» or «the cessation of» something.
fact: Cessation means the stopping or ending of something.
fact: «Cessation of hostilities» means that fighting stops.
fact: «Smoking cessation» means stopping smoking.
fact: Cessation is a formal word. In everyday talk, people say stop or end.
fact: Cessation is a noun, and its plural is cessations.
exercise: «The cessation of the rain let the children play outside.» What does cessation mean here? | The sound of thunder | The colour of the sky | *The stopping of the rain | The start of a big storm
exercise: «The leaders agreed on a cessation of hostilities, so the fighting stopped.» What does cessation of hostilities mean? | A party for the winners | *The stopping of fighting | The start of a new war | A long journey to another country
exercise: Which everyday word means the same as cessation? | enjoy | begin | *stop | grow
test: «The cessation of work came at five o'clock.» What does cessation mean? | The beginning of work | The pay for work | *The stopping of work | The place where work is done
test: Which phrase is about stopping smoking? | smoking music | smoking chimney | smoking festival | *smoking cessation
exam: The news said the cessation of the storm meant the roads were safe again. What does cessation mean? | A loud noise | The start of the storm | *The ending of the storm | The name of a town
